{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-action--12","process--explorer-exe","process--netsh-exe","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--be99ba49-e121-58a8-ba7b-dd3de316cfcf","instance--57bd700a-faa2-5f72-95f2-2694bcea17c9","instance--4dfebe3d-6d66-5915-87d0-37e22755ddc7","instance--af4bb520-aae2-56b8-9431-b68721d102a5"],"properties":[["name","XLoader/FormBook encryption analysis and malware decryption"],["description","Analysis of XLoader/FormBook procedures for string, C2, and function decryption, including injected process behavior."],["scope","malware"],["author",[["name","Unknown"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","any.run"],["url","https://any.run/cybersecurity-blog/xloader-formbook-encryption-analysis-and-malware-decryption/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Store encrypted strings in blobs"],["description","Next, let\u2019s investigate how string encryption works in XLoader. All byte arrays containing encrypted strings or key information are \u200b\u200blocated in special kinds of blobs.\n\nAs you can see in the screenshot above, this blob is a function that returns a pointer to itself, below this function are the bytes you are looking for."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Generate string decryption key"],["description","In order to decrypt strings, first a key is generated. The key is generated from 3 parts, to which the above-described functions are applied.\n\nHere K1_blob, K2_blob, and K3_blob are functions that return data from the blocks described above, and the string length is an argument for them.\n\nThe functions VM_Decrypt, RC4_with_sub_Layer and sha1_* are modified algorithms that we discussed earlier."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Decrypt string blob layers"],["description","The strings themselves are also stored as a blob and are covered by two layers of encryption:\n\nVM_decrypt\n\nRC4 that uses the key obtained above.\n\nAt the same time, RC4 is not used for the whole blob at once."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Loop through and decrypt strings"],["description","Consequently, to decrypt the strings, we need to loop through this structure and consistently decrypt all the strings."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Store C2 decoys among decrypted strings"],["description","Along with the encrypted strings, C2 decoys are also stored there. They are always located at the end of all decrypted strings, beginning and ending with the f-start and f-end strings."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1001.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Decrypt main C2 with three RC4 keys"],["description","Next, let\u2019s see how the main C2 encryption works. The main C2 is located elsewhere in the code, so you can get it separately from the C2 decoys.\n\nTo decrypt it, as well as to decrypt the strings, 3 keys are used. The C2 decryption scheme is shown below:\n\nis the encrypted C2\n\nis the decrypted C2\n\nThe algorithm itself is a 3 times sequential application of the RC4 algorithm with 3 different keys."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Inject XLoader into Explorer.exe"],["description","The C2 decoys are decrypted inside the XLoader injected into Explorer.exe."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1055"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Pass XLoader into netsh.exe via APC injection"],["description","And in this case, it is passed to netsh.exe, which also contains XLoader via APC injection."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1055.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Encrypt functions with RC4 and XORed hardcoded key"],["description","It\u2019s actually quite simple. RC4 is used as the encryption algorithm. This time, the key is hardcoded and written right in the code and then xored with the 4-byte gamma."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Locate encrypted functions by boundary markers"],["description","After that, you should find pointers to the start and end of the function. This is how you do it:\u00a0 a unique 4-byte value is placed at the beginning and end of each encrypted function. The XLoader looks for these values and gets the desired pointers."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Recursively decrypt and execute functions"],["description","Then the function is decrypted, control is given to it, and it similarly searches for and decrypts the next function. This happens until the function with the main functionality is decrypted and executed. So, functions should be decrypted recursively."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Collect decoy decryption key parts from two exit points"],["description","The key to decrypting C2 decoys consists of 2 parts and is collected separately at two different exit points. One exit point gets the 20-byte protected key, and the second gets the 4-byte gamma to decrypt the key."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--d765a677-2f34-53a4-bbb7-bac2fd45303c","120":"instance--7ba34b1f-770d-5092-8729-43ed3f06da9a","150":"instance--45e199ed-111c-5f09-8172-d0bc496709c4","180":"instance--2335ef59-f9ec-5317-b4c5-8ffcbe2a5693","210":"instance--cbc4caf2-9fd1-5af0-8dd1-8b17d6ca57f2","240":"instance--d778454e-b2ca-56a7-afc2-7b2fcbb1aef3","270":"instance--cf903daa-03e2-51bf-96e6-617d75181a59","30":"instance--41d7208f-e500-528e-a2e5-f0bfbd855be0","300":"instance--48cd7151-7b73-5ce1-8c3e-38ffe247419b","330":"instance--31b97fa0-1fa9-508f-84c1-f0306952791d","60":"instance--b50c21a9-d9d2-5b30-bf89-7f05f8a74123","90":"instance--029985c5-1496-5a8c-95cc-4090c252e604"},"id":"process","instance":"process--explorer-exe","properties":[["command_line","Explorer.exe"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"The C2 decoys are decrypted inside the XLoader injected into Explorer.exe.","source":"https://any.run/cybersecurity-blog/xloader-formbook-encryption-analysis-and-malware-decryption/"}]]],["display_name","Explorer.exe"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--66ac9786-ffc3-53ce-b011-6dbc9e709141","120":"instance--2ae6bb3f-6b77-51a1-89c5-955030a25c72","150":"instance--5de4049a-89de-5dad-bd30-7267059bcdbb","180":"instance--61efe160-bbd8-54c4-98c9-432b0d2011eb","210":"instance--856d49a9-243b-57bb-9a1a-47e32d898f9b","240":"instance--5cd4f320-4fc5-57eb-be47-f00b8cf0c858","270":"instance--3275c02e-7f9e-5d0f-be97-c794164c809f","30":"instance--d83d8370-70ae-5e00-8e41-e0cb835f1a67","300":"instance--b21255f0-2709-5a56-a2e7-d55b7e8e612b","330":"instance--6faad31e-2ea2-5e24-9886-676c98638099","60":"instance--7b2fd924-cab6-5a9b-b5a0-24541bea0cd0","90":"instance--8d8b0648-0b13-5dd2-9de7-180ab3f1d5b4"},"id":"process","instance":"process--netsh-exe","properties":[["command_line","netsh.exe"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"And in this case, it is passed to netsh.exe, which also contains XLoader via APC injection.","source":"https://any.run/cybersecurity-blog/xloader-formbook-encryption-analysis-and-malware-decryption/"}]]],["display_name","netsh.exe"]]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","latches":[]},{"id":"vertical_anchor","instance":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","latches":[]},{"id":"vertical_anchor","instance":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1","latches":[]},{"id":"vertical_anchor","instance":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","latches":[]},{"id":"vertical_anchor","instance":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","latches":[]},{"id":"vertical_anchor","instance":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","latches":["instance--8a9e95af-9def-5e9b-8ac2-3b9d956ebdc2"]},{"id":"vertical_anchor","instance":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","latches":[]},{"id":"horizontal_anchor","instance":"instance--efe929